From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:50:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 05/45] inkling2: EXL3 loading and the decoder forward on one
 GPU

Loads an exllamav3 pack (the converter's tensor names) on main's shared EXL3 operators:
dense projections through exl3.Dense, the 384 routed experts as one grouped
layer, everything else as stored. Each rank's share is planned already
(whole key heads with their query groups, 128-wide expert and vocab blocks,
input-side cuts on rows) and exercised at one rank for now.

New kernels in inkling2/ops.cu: embedding with its norm, the block
attention-residual mix and the norm after it, row dots (sinks, dynamic conv
taps, router), the router's top-k, the softcapped SwiGLU epilogue, static and
dynamic short convolutions with per-stream state, and the logit softcap.
The experts run main's grouped kernels in Experts.run's order with only the
gate/up epilogue swapped, so the shared kernels are untouched.

tf-inkling2-cuda writes every row's logits for a set of texts, once as a
prompt pass and once as decode rows, for the exllamav3 check.

A truncated pack may hold no global layer, so config no longer refuses that.
